the "roll to hit calculation" is based on this:

        tmp = 1 + Luck + abon() + find_mac(mtmp) + u.uhitinc +
                maybe_polyd(youmonst.data->mlevel, u.ulevel);

and then add the weapon enchantment and the "weapon_hit_bonus", which
is where the skilled/expert etc. comes in.

which is then comapred to a roll of a d20-- if the sum is bigger, you hit.

where 


abon() is your strength/dex bonus
Luck is your luck, which maxes out at 13
find_mac gives you the monster's AC
uhitinc is magical increases to your accuracy [i.e. rings]
and maybe_polyd(youmonst.data->mlevel, u.ulevel) is your level 
    if you aren't polymorphed.


So, assuming you have maxed out luck, str and dex of 18, and 
you aren't polymorphed or wearing a ring of increase accuracy- you get


 1 + 13 + 5+ MONSTER'S AC + YOUR LEVEL + WEAPON_ENCHANT + SKILL BONUS

= 19 + MONSTER'S AC + YOUR LEVEL + WEAPON_ENCHANT + SKILL BONUS 

Now, the best monster AC I can find in the spoilers is -10-- but monsters
can wear armor and stuff on top of that, so lets say -20.  So if you are 
level 21, have a +7 weapon, and a -7 skill bonus, against a monster of 
AC -20, it doesn't matter..

As your level goes even higher, it matters even less..

So basically-- at the start of the game, a -7 to hit penalty will kill you-
by the end, its mostly a moot point.

